1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:04,940
Every evening, before I lock up, I tell my phone how the day went.

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:07,470
[voice note] Today I sold GH₵2,400:

3
00:00:07,470 --> 00:00:09,910
[voice note] GH₵900 cash, GH₵1,200 MoMo,

4
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:12,370
[voice note] and Kojo still owes GH₵300.

5
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:14,670
[voice note] I bought GH₵700 of stock with cash,

6
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:16,070
[voice note] paid GH₵80 delivery,

7
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:18,470
[voice note] moved GH₵500 from bank to MoMo,

8
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:21,010
[voice note] Abena paid GH₵200 of what she owed into MoMo,

9
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:23,400
[voice note] and I took GH₵150 cash home.

10
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,220
No forms. No accounting words.

11
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:29,550
Busy with a customer? I type it as it happens.

12
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,420
CashNarra turns my words into records.

13
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:37,070
It asks what I left out. Which account paid for delivery?

14
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:40,460
MoMo. I check all eight, and I save.

15
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:45,420
Abena’s GH₵200 is not a new sale. She owes GH₵400 now.

16
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:47,520
Kojo still owes GH₵300.

17
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:51,930
GH₵2,300 came in. GH₵930 went out.

18
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:55,520
My day. My words. My numbers.

19
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:58,120
Tell your money story. See the numbers.

20
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,540
Coming soon.

